.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt DTFL_TRACE_SET_LOGICAL_COMPACTION 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_trace_set_logical_compaction ,
.Nm dtfl_trace_set_physical_compaction ,
.Nm dtfl_trace_logical_compaction ,
.Nm dtfl_trace_physical_compaction
.Nd advance or read a trace handle's compaction holds
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/arrange.h
.Ft void
.Fo dtfl_trace_set_logical_compaction
.Fa "dtfl_trace *t" "const uint64_t *frontier" "size_t n"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo dtfl_trace_set_physical_compaction
.Fa "dtfl_trace *t" "const uint64_t *frontier" "size_t n"
.Fc
.Ft const uint64_t *
.Fn dtfl_trace_logical_compaction "const dtfl_trace *t" "size_t *n"
.Ft const uint64_t *
.Fn dtfl_trace_physical_compaction "const dtfl_trace *t" "size_t *n"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A trace handle from
.Xr dtfl_arranged_trace 3
is a reader of a shared trace, and each reader holds the trace back at
two frontiers.
The trace may not forget history that any reader's holds still need, so
a handle that never advances its holds keeps every update at its
original time for as long as the handle lives.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_trace_set_logical_compaction
advances the logical hold.
Once every reader is past a time, the trace may rewrite the times of
updates not beyond the frontier to representative times, which lets it
merge equivalent updates and keep its memory bounded over an unbounded
history.
History before the frontier can then only be read in accumulation, not
at its original times.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_trace_set_physical_compaction
advances the physical hold, which lets the trace merge batches.
After it,
.Xr dtfl_trace_to_vec_through 3
can cut the trace only at frontiers beyond the new hold.
.Pp
In both setters
.Fa frontier
is an antichain of
.Fa n
times, each as wide as the trace's time class, stored contiguously.
As in differential dataflow, the new hold is the join of the current
hold and
.Fa frontier ,
so passing a frontier behind the current hold does not move it back.
An empty frontier
.Pq Fa n No is 0
releases the hold completely.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_trace_logical_compaction
and
.Fn dtfl_trace_physical_compaction
return the current hold as a contiguous antichain and store its length
in
.Fa *n .
The pointer is valid until the next call that sets that hold, or until
the handle is freed.
.Pp
Freeing a handle with
.Xr dtfl_trace_free 3
releases both of its holds.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The setters return no value.
The getters return the hold, or
.Dv NULL
with
.Fa *n
set to 0 when the hold is empty.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A long-running maintained view keeps a reader for point-in-time reads.
After commit
.Va n
is fully applied and no reader needs an older snapshot, advance both
holds to
.Va n
so the trace can compact everything before it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint64_t f = n;

dtfl_trace_set_logical_compaction(t, &f, 1);
dtfl_trace_set_physical_compaction(t, &f, 1);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_arranged_trace 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_trace_free 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_trace_to_vec_through 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of differential dataflow's
.Fn TraceReader::set_logical_compaction ,
.Fn set_physical_compaction ,
.Fn get_logical_compaction
and
.Fn get_physical_compaction
on a
.Vt TraceAgent
.Pq Pa trace/mod.rs , Pa operators/arrange/agent.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The trace handle belongs to the worker thread that created it.
A trace is worker-local; it is not shared across threads.
